# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Env / secrets
.env
.env.*

# Recorded model transcripts and local run artifacts (M0.4/M0.5), plus the
# checker's own output when dogfooding this repo (M7.3) — all regenerated from
# the current review, none of it a source file.
.acceptance/*
# ...except the checker's ignore config (#105), which is input rather than
# output. It is the only committed thing under here, and it must stay committed:
# a fresh clone or a CI run without it puts each dogfood run's own output.log
# into the diff that run is reviewing, and the review then cannot be replayed.
!.acceptance/ignore
*.local

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Dogfood runs (`dogfood-logs/`) and `session-state.md` are COMMITTED, not
# ignored. A dogfood run saved with its inputs and its judgement is a candidate
# benchmark case — that is exactly what `tests/fixtures/rating-stability/` is,
# and it could only be turned into one (#190) because those inputs survived.

# Claude handoff notes — rolling, disposable, never committed
handoff*.md
.claude/settings.local.json
